  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "Consider the differential equation \n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2033}-9y={x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe corresponding homogeneous equation has the fundamental solutions ${y}_{1}(x)={e}^{3x}$ and ${y}_{2}(x)={e}^{-3x}.$ \n\nAccording to the method of variation of parameters, we should seek a particular solution \n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)={u}_{1}(x){y}_{1}+{u}_{2}(x){y}_{2}\n$$\n\nthat satisfies the following constraints:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1}^{\u2032}{y}_{1}^{\u2032}+{u}_{2}^{\u2032}{y}_{2}^{\u2032}={x}^{2} \\\\ {u}_{1}^{\u2032}{y}_{1}+{u}_{2}^{\u2032}{y}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that ${u}_{1}(x)=\\int g(x)\\,\\text{d}x,$ find the function $g.$",
